& [PrunedSurface] is closed
  + [P01] comparison-scope identity is pruned because complete structural scope equality is stronger and cannot hide unequal coordinates
  + [P02] IncompleteClaimed and FaultedClaimed are pruned because profile 0.1 derives only from two CompleteClaimed lineages
  + [P03] a peer assembly field is pruned because the ordered digest carrier already owns its complete assembly ancestry
  + [P04] bare digest, loose assembly, locator, key, lazy lookup, and caller summary inputs are pruned
  + [P05] clocks, ticks, timestamps, durations, deadlines, freshness, and numeric order fields are pruned
  + [P06] admitted lineage, producer capability, sealed producer trait, token, key, registry, secret, and production fixture constructor are deferred wholly to separately sourced M2C
  + [P07] Capability fault is pruned because profile 0.1 exposes no production-admission operation
  + [P08] OsSnapshotProven, quiescence, stability, atomicity, immutability, current truth, and stronger evidence grades are pruned
  + [P09] direct TopologyReceipt conversion, issuance, signing, ledger, consumption, freshness, single use, admission, and mutation are pruned
  + [P10] open enums, catch-all maps, aliases, defaults, flattening, untagged decoding, arbitrary JSON, and free diagnostics are pruned
  + [P11] public mutable result fields, Deserialize, Default, From, Into, and unrestricted result construction are pruned
  + [P12] platform, filesystem, clock, random, process, environment, network, persistence, database, Git runtime, model, tool, fixture-execution, neural, distributed, and FPGA surfaces are pruned
  + [P13] dependency, Cargo, lockfile, unsafe, and second-module growth are pruned
  + [P14] implementation, execution, producer, physical, issuer, and consumer authority are pruned until later exact signatures

& [BoundedGrowth] admits only proof-support structure
  + [G01] one nonzero-u64 AcquisitionIdentity wrapper for logical correlation without generation or uniqueness claims
  + [G02] one complete AcquisitionScopeClaim product with structural equality and exact current profile coordinates
  + [G03] one role-independent AcquisitionLineageClaim owning identity, scope, CompleteClaimed, and complete current digest-carrier ancestry
  + [G04] one OrderedAcquisitionPairClaim owning exactly First and Second lineages plus an explicit identity-bound causal relation
  + [G05] one RepeatedInventoryEvidencePlan binding exact current reconciliation and requesting only NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + [G06] one output-only RepeatedInventoryEvidenceClaim retaining pair, reconciliation input and result, evidence grade, and ClaimOnly provenance
  + [G07] one closed ten-code fault family with one bounded field and message and no partial output
  + [G08] static API evidence proving producer-admitted, issuer, receipt-conversion, and effect surfaces are absent

& [ThreatModel] challenges authority and data boundaries
  + [T01_identity_forgery] caller chooses two nonzero unequal values and claims two events; structural validity still proves neither occurrence nor uniqueness
  + [T02_identity_collision] two actual producers could reuse a logical value; M2C must govern the collision domain and cannot cite this wrapper as a generator
  + [T03_scope_laundering] caller changes one coordinate while preserving a label or digest; complete structural equality refuses the pair
  + [T04_carrier_substitution] first carrier is reused for second or peer ancestry is swapped; role-owned complete carriers and independent rederivation refuse substitution
  + [T05_digest_tamper] retained digest text changes while ancestry remains; current rederivation refuses the lineage
  + [T06_causal_laundering] JSON order, field position, left-right operands, or increasing identity is cited as time; exact endpoints and relation kind still remain a ClaimOnly declaration
  + [T07_equal_inflation] two supplied carriers reconcile Equal; no acquisition, causal truth, quiescence, snapshot, freshness, or current-world claim follows
  + [T08_serde_laundering] strict decoded forms are called admitted; producer-admitted types and construction routes do not exist in profile 0.1
  + [T09_output_laundering] serialized ClaimOnly output is replayed as authority; Deserialize and receipt conversion are absent and provenance grade remains explicit
  + [T10_fixture_laundering] synthetic builders escape into production; only cfg(test) helpers or ordinary pure claim derivation are allowed and static tests police the public surface
  + [T11_profile_downgrade] stale nested profile is accepted as compatible; exact current validators reject without alias or migration
  + [T12_fault_smuggling] partial accepted lineage accompanies a denial; every failure returns one atomic bounded fault and no result
  + [T13_resource_pressure] nested values exploit unbounded collections or diagnostics; exactly two lineages inherit current bounds and new fields are scalar or fixed closed enums
  + [T14_authority_creep] implementation convenience adds producer or effect code; artifact diff and one-module zero-effect lock stop processing

& [DualHemisphereReview] converges
  + constructive hemisphere retains the smallest useful correlation, scope, lineage, order, reconciliation, and ClaimOnly result graph
  + adversarial hemisphere finds no path from public decode, pure validation, pure rederivation, Equal, or serialization to physical provenance
  + independent roles remain source author, SJS processor, claim author, pure validator, pure derive function, synthetic test builder, future M2C producer, future issuer, future receipt issuer, and future consumer
  + every threat has a denial in C01 through C24 or an explicit later-authority dependency

